# Work Progress

## Initial Planning

The original concept was to develop a robotic arm-based 2D plotter capable of reproducing vector drawings. The intended workflow was to convert an image into a vector graphic using Inkscape, generate G-code from the vector drawing, and use the generated commands to control the plotter.

To achieve precise positioning, BLDC motors with magnetic angle sensors were selected. The feedback provided by these sensors would allow the controller to continuously estimate the position of the robotic arm and move the end effector to a desired (x, y) coordinate.

### Accomplishments

* Researched existing plotter and robotic arm designs
* Defined overall system workflow
* Identified hardware requirements
* Selected BLDC motors due to their torque and feedback capabilities
* Established project milestones and development goals

### Initial Goals

* Achieve accurate X-Y positioning
* Implement closed-loop motor control
* Reduce vibration during movement
* Improve trajectory smoothness
* Develop stable and repeatable motion

